  "term": "ischemic penumbra",
  "definition": "Ischemic penumbra is brain tissue around the core of a stroke that has too little blood flow to work normally but is still alive. This tissue can recover if blood flow is restored, but without reperfusion it is likely to die and become part of the infarct.",
